08:25:20 said  Map Local and Breakpoints now use the same easy pattern as Proxyman: a clean rule table, a focused editor popup, and a live URL tester before you turn anything on. You can also click **Mock this** or **Catch this** on any request in the inspector, and it will fill in the rule for you — or edit the rule that already matches.
08:25:20 said  Yes, `*` works for query rules. It matches anything, including `?` and `&`, so a pattern like `*/v1/products?*` matches any query string, while `*/v1/products?limit=20*` matches only that query. A `?` on its own stays literal, so the patterns are easier to write.
08:25:20 said  The app now shows which rules match a selected request, catches only matching traffic instead of every request, and includes a wildcard cheat sheet with “Try” examples. The build, three unit tests, screenshots, and the rebuild check all pass; the only remaining uncertainty is exact visual matching, since I can read the layout and text but cannot see the images directly.
